Subject: [PATCH] devtools: a keep-alive switch outlives the last window

--aliasmode-keep-alive keeps the browser process running after its last
window closes, with no window and no tray icon, until Browser.close or
the end of the process. The launcher uses the time to read the profile's
cookies and storage over the remote debugging connection when the user
closes the last window, which on Windows and Linux ends the browser.

It takes the keep-alive Chromium already takes for --no-startup-window
and --headless when the browser runs with --remote-debugging-port or
--remote-debugging-pipe, so it has no effect without one of them. Unlike
--no-startup-window, the startup window opens and the last session is
restored as usual. Pages see nothing.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/devtools/chrome_devtools_manager_delegate.cc b/chrome/browser/devtools/chrome_devtools_manager_delegate.cc
index 37a8337..fee8948 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/devtools/chrome_devtools_manager_delegate.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/devtools/chrome_devtools_manager_delegate.cc
@@ -86,6 +86,13 @@ const char ChromeDevToolsManagerDelegate::kTypePage[] = "page";
 
 namespace {
 
+// AliasMode: --aliasmode-keep-alive keeps the browser running after its last
+// window closes, as --no-startup-window does, so the launcher can still read
+// the profile over the remote debugging connection before it closes the
+// browser with Browser.close. The startup window and session restore stay as
+// they are. Pages see nothing.
+constexpr char kAliasModeKeepAlive[] = "aliasmode-keep-alive";
+
 // LINT.IfChange(DevToolsRemoteDebuggingConnectionPermission)
 // This enum is used for UMA histograms and should not be renumbered.
 enum class DevToolsRemoteDebuggingConnectionPermission {
@@ -194,8 +201,11 @@ ChromeDevToolsManagerDelegate::ChromeDevToolsManagerDelegate() {
   // manager daemon. The extra keep alive is not needed and makes ChromeOS
   // not able to shutdown chrome properly. See https://crbug.com/40167603.
   base::CommandLine* command_line = base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess();
+  // AliasMode: --aliasmode-keep-alive takes the same keep-alive with a
+  // startup window, so the browser outlives its last window.
   if ((command_line->HasSwitch(switches::kNoStartupWindow) ||
-       command_line->HasSwitch(switches::kHeadless)) &&
+       command_line->HasSwitch(switches::kHeadless) ||
+       command_line->HasSwitch(kAliasModeKeepAlive)) &&
       (command_line->HasSwitch(switches::kRemoteDebuggingPipe) ||
        command_line->HasSwitch(switches::kRemoteDebuggingPort))) {
     // If running without a startup window with remote debugging,
